# Africa Web3 Institute (AWI) Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
The goal is to develop a premium, policy-oriented, Web3-inspired landing page for the Africa Web3 Institute. The design must be clean, authoritative, and structured like a "policy engine with a builder's pulse." Essential aesthetics include a white background, "Deep Policy Blue" headlines, "Digital Gold" accents, and "Pan-African Green" interactive elements like buttons.

## Proposed Changes

### Configuration
We will create the required web stack files in the `c:\Users\Administrator\African W3 landing page` directory. 

#### [NEW] `index.html`
Contains the complete semantic structure corresponding to the 11-part wireframe specified.
#### [NEW] `styles.css`
Implementation of the 8pt spacing grid, design tokens (colors, variants of Inter font weight, shadows), and CSS grid/flexbox layouts. Responsive breakpoints will ensure the page adapts to mobile, tablet, and desktop up to a max container width of 1200px.
#### [NEW] `script.js`
Minor utilities for a sticky header, mobile navigation drawer, and potentially smooth transitions/scroll behaviors or dynamic hover effects described in the wireframe.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Validate HTML semantics using external tools if necessary.
- Locally run `python -m http.server` and visually inspect the page across various viewport sizes.
### Manual Verification
- Review against Figma UI specs provided (Color Tokens, Spacing, Font scale).
- Verify hover animations and card grid configurations match the described behavior ("TranslateY(-4px)").
